@Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7270

### 1. Prime the CSRF cookie - run this first, every session.
# The response Set-Cookie header carries "XSRF-TOKEN=<value>". Copy <value> into @csrfToken below.
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/csrf-token

###

@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_XSRF-TOKEN_COOKIE_VALUE

### 2. Register a new account. Sends a confirmation email (logged, not sent - see step 3).
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass1!"
}

###

@confirmationToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_LOG_OUTPUT

### 3. Confirm the email using the token logged by step 2 (see LoggingEmailSender). Login is
### blocked - RequireConfirmedEmail - until this runs; step 4 fails with 400 EmailNotConfirmed
### without it.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/confirm-email
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "token": "{{confirmationToken}}"
}

###

### 4. Log in. Sets access_token + refresh_token as HttpOnly cookies.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass1!"
}

### 5. Get the current user, resolved from the access_token cookie.
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/me

###

### 6. Rotate the refresh token (also issues a fresh access token).
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/refresh
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

###

### 7. Change password while logged in (requires the access_token cookie from step 4).
# On success this revokes every session for the account, including the one making this call -
# the access_token/refresh_token cookies captured so far stop working right after this request.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "currentPassword": "StrongPass1!",
  "newPassword": "EvenStrongerPass1!"
}

###

### 8. Request a password reset. Always 204, regardless of whether the email is registered.
# No email provider is configured yet - the reset link is logged instead (see LoggingEmailSender).
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

###

@resetToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_LOG_OUTPUT

### 9. Reset the password using the token from step 8.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "AnotherStrongPass1!"
}

###

### 10. Log out. Revokes the refresh token server-side and clears both cookies (harmless no-op if
### the session was already killed by step 7's change-password).
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/authentication/logout
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

###
